  "body": "Stacked on #791\n\nBranched from #791's head `40f256b4` (`issue/672-plasma-laws-2`); until #791 merges, this PR's diff also shows its commits - the new work is the single commit on top. Fork synced at v0.17.0.\n\n## What changed\nFollow-ups from the three reviews of #791 (#672 step 2). Decisions in `docs/decisions/801-plasma-followups.md`.\n\n1. **Tip-up over a freed hole slug** (`sim::verify::plasma`). A rapid is now judged against every earlier closed ring, not only OUTER ones; a hit on a hole is `TipUp { slug: true }`, read \"crosses the slug of hole C<n>\". No slug-size floor (whether a slug drops depends on the slat pitch, which the program does not know; the finding is a warning). The rapid leaving the hole just cut starts on its own slug (a hole's lead-out ends on the scrap side), so its first stretch is the departure and is not judged against that hole; a later stretch back over the slug is.\n2. **The reverse inside-part crossing.** When the later cut is OUTER, an earlier ring with a stretch strictly inside it that it does not strictly enclose is a `CutCrossing` (L cut first, then E around it). INNER is left alone, so a nested part touching its hole's wall, cut first, stays common-line legal.\n3. **Inch and G41/G42 at the gate** (`plasma_gate`). An inch document reads clean, and a cut crossing blocks the post with its place in inches (mm in a mm document). A control-compensated program is judged on its torch-centre moves (same rings as the computer-offset program) and the same cuts laid outline-first are refused.\n4. **The vacuous diamond-hole pin** is replaced by a nested part touching its hole's wall, cut first, which reaches the laws (kerf warning only).\n5. **Decision 4a** now states plainly that the 2r cap refuses a normal-sized inside V sharper than about 30 degrees; pinned by a 20 mm, 25-degree V refused.\n6. **Zero-width slit.** `Region::new` keeps area, so an out-and-back spike in a picked contour vanished and the plate generated as the plain rectangle. `Region::new` is right for regions (milling asks for area) and is unchanged, so no geo2d issue is filed. The plasma contour door (`motion::plasma::nest::contours`) now refuses, by name and place, a picked vertex the normalised ring no longer reaches (\"pick the slit as an open run\"). A collinear vertex the region drops stays legal.\n\n## How tested\nPins (each refusal removed and the pin seen to fail, then restored):\n\n| Removed | Fails |\n|---|---|\n| slug tip-up (filter back to OUTER) | sim `plasma_laws::a_rapid_over_a_freed_hole_slug_is_a_tip_up_naming_the_hole`, `a_rapid_leaving_a_hole_and_running_back_over_its_slug_is_a_tip_up`; sim `plasma_program::a_rapid_over_a_freed_hole_slug_is_read_and_warned` |\n| departure exemption | the two `plasma_laws` slug tests above |\n| reverse crossing | `plasma_laws::a_part_cut_around_an_earlier_ring_running_through_it_is_refused` |\n| slit refusal | motion `plasma::tests::a_zero_width_slit_in_a_picked_contour_is_refused_not_dropped` |\n| document units in `posting_plasma::describe` | app `plasma_gate::an_inch_document_is_judged_the_same_and_placed_in_inches` |\n| plasma refusals as gate problems | app `plasma_gate`: the two inch/G41-G42 pins plus the two existing refusal pins |\n\nAlso new: motion `plasma::tests::a_normal_sized_v_sharper_than_30_degrees_is_refused`; `plasma_laws::a_ring_inside_an_earlier_part_touching_its_edge_is_refused` now uses the reaching fixture.\n\nLocal: sim `plasma_laws` 21/21, `plasma_program` 6/6; motion `plasma::tests` 16/16; app `plasma_gate` 6/6, `plasma_profile` 7/7, `conformance` 6/6; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. Linux quick gate (`--base upstream/main`) on 873c76b4: sim, motion and app suites green, 0 failed (3.4 min).\n\n## Not exercised\n- No real-table check of how slugs actually drop; the no-floor rule is a reasoned default (decision 1).\n- The slit refusal is pinned on an axis-aligned spike; near-zero-width (not exact) slits still reach the cover law and its 2r cap as before.\n- UI and MCP surfaces: no change (they read the same gate).\n- `crates/sim/tests/plasma_laws.rs` is 404 lines (a test file just over the ~400 guideline).\n\nChangelog: Plasma laws warn on a rapid over a freed hole slug, refuse an earlier ring running through a later part, and the plasma profile refuses a zero-width slit in a picked contour instead of dropping it.\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #801\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
